    "question": {
      ":question/id": "af92164c-129c-55a0-a9ce-6f63375d7f3a",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Given $\\mathbf{f}(t)=⟨- 2 t^{3} - 1,\\,3 t + 3,\\,- t^{2} - 1⟩$, find $(\\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}\\times \\mathbf{f})^{\\prime}(t).$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the cross product rule, preserving the factor order:\n\n$$\n(\\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}\\times \\mathbf{f})^{\\prime}(t)=\\mathbf{f}^{\\prime\\prime}(t)\\times \\mathbf{f}(t)+\\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}(t)\\times \\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}(t)\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}_{1}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(- 2 t^{3} - 1)=- 6 t^{2} \\\\ \\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}_{2}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(3 t + 3)=3 \\\\ \\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}_{3}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(- t^{2} - 1)=- 2 t \\\\ \\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}(t) & =⟨- 6 t^{2},\\,3,\\,- 2 t⟩ \\\\ \\mathbf{f}^{\\prime\\prime}_{1}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(- 6 t^{2})=- 12 t \\\\ \\mathbf{f}^{\\prime\\prime}_{2}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(3)=0 \\\\ \\mathbf{f}^{\\prime\\prime}_{3}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(- 2 t)=-2 \\\\ \\mathbf{f}^{\\prime\\prime}(t) & =⟨- 12 t,\\,0,\\,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the first product-rule term and the second product-rule term, denoted $P_1$ and $P_2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P_1 & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ - 12 t & 0 & -2 \\\\ - 2 t^{3} - 1 & 3 t + 3 & - t^{2} - 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ P_{1,1} & =\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -2 \\\\ 3 t + 3 & - t^{2} - 1\\end{vmatrix}=6 t + 6 \\\\ P_{1,2} & =-\\begin{vmatrix}- 12 t & -2 \\\\ - 2 t^{3} - 1 & - t^{2} - 1\\end{vmatrix}=- 8 t^{3} - 12 t + 2 \\\\ P_{1,3} & =\\begin{vmatrix}- 12 t & 0 \\\\ - 2 t^{3} - 1 & 3 t + 3\\end{vmatrix}=- 36 t^{2} - 36 t \\\\ P_1 & =⟨6 t + 6,\\,- 8 t^{3} - 12 t + 2,\\,- 36 t^{2} - 36 t⟩ \\\\ P_2 & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ - 6 t^{2} & 3 & - 2 t \\\\ - 6 t^{2} & 3 & - 2 t\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ P_{2,1} & =\\begin{vmatrix}3 & - 2 t \\\\ 3 & - 2 t\\end{vmatrix}=0 \\\\ P_{2,2} & =-\\begin{vmatrix}- 6 t^{2} & - 2 t \\\\ - 6 t^{2} & - 2 t\\end{vmatrix}=0 \\\\ P_{2,3} & =\\begin{vmatrix}- 6 t^{2} & 3 \\\\ - 6 t^{2} & 3\\end{vmatrix}=0 \\\\ P_2 & =⟨0,\\,0,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the two terms componentwise:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}\\times \\mathbf{f})^{\\prime}(t) & =P_1+P_2 \\\\  & =⟨6 t + 6,\\,- 8 t^{3} - 12 t + 2,\\,- 36 t^{2} - 36 t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
