    "question": {
      ":question/id": "0610e3b4-0a22-5776-ba1b-9b6660d33166",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Find $(\\mathbf{f}\\times \\mathbf{g})^{\\prime}(t)$ given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{f}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}t^{2} \\\\ -2 \\\\ t - 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\mathbf{g}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}t - 3 \\\\ - 3 t \\\\ t^{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the cross product rule, preserving the factor order:\n\n$$\n(\\mathbf{f}\\times \\mathbf{g})^{\\prime}(t)=\\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}(t)\\times \\mathbf{g}(t)+\\mathbf{f}(t)\\times \\mathbf{g}^{\\prime}(t)\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}_{1}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t^{2})=2 t \\\\ \\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}_{2}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(-2)=0 \\\\ \\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}_{3}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t - 3)=1 \\\\ \\mathbf{f}^{\\prime}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 t \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\mathbf{g}^{\\prime}_{1}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t - 3)=1 \\\\ \\mathbf{g}^{\\prime}_{2}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(- 3 t)=-3 \\\\ \\mathbf{g}^{\\prime}_{3}(t) & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t^{2})=2 t \\\\ \\mathbf{g}^{\\prime}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2 t\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the first product-rule term and the second product-rule term, denoted $P_1$ and $P_2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P_1 & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 2 t & 0 & 1 \\\\ t - 3 & - 3 t & t^{2}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ P_{1,1} & =\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ - 3 t & t^{2}\\end{vmatrix}=3 t \\\\ P_{1,2} & =-\\begin{vmatrix}2 t & 1 \\\\ t - 3 & t^{2}\\end{vmatrix}=- 2 t^{3} + t - 3 \\\\ P_{1,3} & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 t & 0 \\\\ t - 3 & - 3 t\\end{vmatrix}=- 6 t^{2} \\\\ P_1 & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 t \\\\ - 2 t^{3} + t - 3 \\\\ - 6 t^{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ P_2 & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ t^{2} & -2 & t - 3 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 2 t\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ P_{2,1} & =\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & t - 3 \\\\ -3 & 2 t\\end{vmatrix}=- t - 9 \\\\ P_{2,2} & =-\\begin{vmatrix}t^{2} & t - 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 t\\end{vmatrix}=- 2 t^{3} + t - 3 \\\\ P_{2,3} & =\\begin{vmatrix}t^{2} & -2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{vmatrix}=2 - 3 t^{2} \\\\ P_2 & =\\begin{bmatrix}- t - 9 \\\\ - 2 t^{3} + t - 3 \\\\ 2 - 3 t^{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the two terms componentwise:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\mathbf{f}\\times \\mathbf{g})^{\\prime}(t) & =P_1+P_2 \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 t - 9 \\\\ - 4 t^{3} + 2 t - 6 \\\\ 2 - 9 t^{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
